Files whose lines end with a lone CR (classic Mac OS) are read as if each CR were a line break,
in every engine: line counts and line ranges count them, the header comment ends at its line,
and no raw CR is printed. A CR before an LF is one line break, so a mix of both counts each once.
== args
input/cr.js
input/cr.md
input/cr.yaml
input/cr.rs
input/cr.css
input/mixed.toml
== file input/cr.js escaped
// Header\rfunction a() {}\rfunction b() {}\r\
== file input/cr.md escaped
---\rdescription: CR doc\r---\r# Title\r\r## Section\r\
== file input/cr.yaml escaped
# Workflow\rname: CI\ron: push\r\
== file input/cr.rs escaped
//! Crate.\r\rpub fn a() {}\rpub struct B;\r\
== file input/cr.css escaped
/* Styles */\r.a { color: red }\r.b { color: blue }\r\
== file input/mixed.toml escaped
a = 1\r\nb = 2\rc = 3\n\
